WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:06.260
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.450
<i>Chikara to chikara butsukareba,
When power collides with power,</i>

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.040
<i>arasoi wa hajimaru.
wars start.</i>

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.590
<i>Tatakau koto ga</i> yuuki <i>to</i>
I <i>don't think fighting</i>

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.590
<i>omowanai kedo...
equals bravery, but...</i>

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.990
<i>...mamoritai yo
...I want to protect</i>

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.550
kimi <i>no sono egao.
that smile on your face.</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.160
<i>Asu e no geeto
We can't see the gate</i>

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.860
<i>mienai keredo...
to tomorrow, but...</i>

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.640
<i>dare ni</i> demo <i>aru yo.
one's inside each of us.</i>

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.300
<i>Let's open the gate!</i>

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.010
Kinou <i>no namida</i> wa
<i>The tears we shed yesterday</i>

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.280
<i>kitto muda ja nai.
are probably not in vain.</i>

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.650
<i>Arasoi no nai</i> mirai wa
<i>A future without war</i>

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.420
<i>ano tobira no mukougawa.
waits behind that door.</i>

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.560
Mune <i>no oku</i> fukaku
<i>Retrieve the key lying</i>

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.500
<i>Jitto shimaikonda
deep inside your heart,</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.300
<i>kagi wo takaku kakagete,
hold it up high,</i>

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.530
<i>fumidasou!
and step out!</i>

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:15.840
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:22.370
<i>You can open the gate!</i>

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.920
Yes. You should take it
easy once in awhile.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.160
However, your vacation ends
tomorrow, does it not?

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.160
There is nothing
to worry about here.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.860
Yes...

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.890
Are you sure you don't want to
watch tomorrow's race in person?

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.870
Yes...

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.210
What did you say?! Ms. Ochiai...

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.770
...please explain
that to me in detail.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.680
<i>Yes, sir. Well, I'm
only in the way here, so...</i>

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.150
No, I mean explain about the
young man named Nishiya.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.160
<i>Oh, him! He looks quite
perturbed before the race.</i>

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.450
<i>He is also treating Mami coldly.
She says the change happened...</i>

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.260
<i>immediately after he returned
from a business trip half a year ago.</i>

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.130
<i>How can I explain...
People can change easily, I guess.</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.860
<i>Um, well, I'l! be heading back now!</i>

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.100
No.
Yes?

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.170
INVADER RESEARCH REPORT 9TH EDITION
Something bothers me about this.
I will come get you.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.460
ALL JAPAN GRAND PRIX

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:52.490
Don't get in my way, dammit!
I'm... I'm number one!!

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.030
What the hell?!

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.710
What's this close ratio transmission crap?!
You sure it isn't CRAWL mission?!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.310
Sorry, sir.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.520
However, you brought it in...

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.930
Making excuses?! I'm Number One!
Do you people understand that?!

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.760
Stop it! That's enough!
Please leave them alone!

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.800
You butt out!

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.940
Who are you?

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.940
This is the principal
at the school I work at.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:42.570
This is my friend from university,
Mami Takigawa, and her fiance, Mr. Nishiya.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.410
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.950
Your car is quite
a fine tuned machine.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.320
Of course it is. I'm Number One.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.790
How does it run?

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.920
Horribly! In the meantime...

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.260
...the other cars sound great.
They're in their best form.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.560
So, you can understand how well
engines run from sound alone?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:05.570
Of course I can. You don't have time
to look at a tachometer during a race.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.970
You have to learn
engine speed by ear.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.170
If your hearing is
that finely-attuned...

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.770
...you can probably hear
sounds inaudible to others.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.510
Now that you mention it, you've
been tossing and turning recently...

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.520
...saying you hear a strange voice.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.680
A strange voice?
Shut your blabbering mouth!

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.490
I'm sorry...

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:29.690
Please excuse the interruption.
I wish you the best of luck in tomorrow's race.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.470
What's with that guy?

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:36.590
He came all this way to show his support.
You don't have to be that way.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.800
I don't like him!

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:42.540
There's a lot riding on this race.
You must be tense.

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.580
Tense? I...

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.740
up

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.380
I can hear it.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.980
I can hear that sound.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.550
Hey, where are you going?

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.650
Going... after him!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.920
Hey, aren't you forgetting something?!

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.430
After him!

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.470
Kill him!

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.210
Wait! What's going on?

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.640
Kill him, kill him!

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.580
What?!
What's the matter?!

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.090
This car is so comfortable,
it's like riding on a cloud.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.030
Ms. Ochiai.
Yes, sir?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.430
Contact home base.
Yes...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.400
Huh? Uh, yes, sir!!

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:45.170
I'm afraid I am right.
Nishiya is an invader.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.430
What?! He can't be.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:51.440
After all, Nishiya has been friends
with Mami since elementary school.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:55.040
And she's even shown me pictures
of him in a photo album. Besides...

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.240
Ms. Ochiai.
In any event, contact the base.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.120
Yes, sir.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.860
Registering paranormal frequenciesl!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.390
Hold om!

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.670
AEGIS home base! AEGIS home base!
It's no good, I can't get through!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.520
Open the glove compartment!

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.210
Yes, sir!

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.280
You know how to use it, I trust?!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.690
Yes, but only in practice...

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.250
lf so, this is the first time
you use one in actual combat!

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.660
Yes, sir...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.940
He gave up...

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:12.290
<i>That number.!</i>

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.360
Mr. Nishiya?!
Fire, Ms. Ochiai!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.810
Commander!

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.810
Don't talk!
You'll bite on your tongue!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.410
Damn.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.760
MEDICAL ROOM

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.230
Excuse me!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.860
Ukiya...

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.730
Huh? What're you doing in
the medical room, Rurippe?

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:02.610
Oh, that. I was asked to replace
Ms. Ochai while she's on vacation.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.570
What is it? Are you hurt?

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.310
Uh, yeah.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.210
That hurts!

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.250
It looks like the
commander went with her.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.910
The commander went
with Ms. Ochiai, eh?

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.650
Maybe they're taking a leisurely
drive somewhere together right now.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.710
What did the boys have for P.E.?

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.730
Huh? Soccer.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.560
The other day, Kaoru taught me a deadly
technique called a "submarine shoot"...

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.900
...sol thought I'd
give it a shot, but...

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.670
Hmm...
You learned it from Kaoru, huh?

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.330
OW- Ow. ow!!

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.210
Be strong.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.300
Heal it with your Gate of Life.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.010
Forget it.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.760
It looks like we escaped with
nothing more than this flat tire.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.630
What a relief. That means
we can make it back...

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.970
No, the invader will come
after us with dogged persistence.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.600
"The invader"?

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.940
I'm sorry. It's likely
that he is after me...

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:14.670
...because I know his true identity.
I'm sorryl got you involved.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.580
That's not what I meant.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.580
You talk about him as though
he's just another invader...

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.610
It's different. He...
I'm certain that he is...

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:30.690
Yes. He resembles the man
who was once Nishiya!

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.790
In other words, he is
an infiltrator! An invader!

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:40.540
The type-Fukuoka invader
earned a fake registration...

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:44.940
...and infiltrated human society.
You remember, don't you?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.310
Yes.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.280
However, this type is different.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:53.980
Without witnesses, he eliminated the real
Nishiya, assumed his form, and then...

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.020
Please stop.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.890
Please, stop it. I beg you.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.890
Ms. Ochiai
Yes, sir?

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:09.060
The invaders are quietly but
surely swelling their numbers.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.400
Now, they are finally beginning
to infiltrate human society...

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:15.930
...by taking the place of
humans in actual existence.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:19.000
I wished to ascertain
that with my own eyes.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:19.910
Yes, sir.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:25.040
It is too cruel a fact to force
Ukiya and the others to confirm.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.680
I can understand.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.310
The report arrived this morning.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.480
Do you mean the Invader
Research Report 9th Edition?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:36.860
Yes. According to it, when they
transform from humans into invaders...

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:41.730
...they are guided by a strange
voice to expose their true form...

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.740
...almost without exception.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.700
A voice?

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.300
I believe that voice is our
so-called "paranormal frequency.”

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:51.400
However, who is behind the
mysterious paranormal frequency?

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.750
What is the trigger
which causes them to act?

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.710
Perhaps...

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.560
Ms. Ochiai, we will now split up.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:44.820
What?

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.870
Take this with you.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.960
It isn't as heavy as you think.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.100
Um, sir. What do you
mean by "split up"?

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:55.770
In the event something
should happen to me...

00:11:55.840 --> 00:12:01.040
...l want you to inform the Far Eastern
branch of what happened here today.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:05.050
Then, I want you to appoint a
stand-in commander immediately...

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:09.920
...without letting the enemy gain headway,
and prepare the troops for action.

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.580
But that's so...

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.120
How can you say something
like that so simply?

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:30.100
Because I have already
died once in my lifetime.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.710
But you're not a ghost.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.610
It happened 24 years ago.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:49.150
I was 17 then,
Captain Ukiya's age.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:53.890
I was a navy air cadet,
assigned to an air force...

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.990
...without being allowed
to complete my training.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:01.960
It was an air force
popularly known as "Divine Thunder."

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:06.170
My grandmother told me about
it once. You don't mean...

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:09.510
Yes. We were the human bombs:
The Ooka.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:13.920
It was May the 4th,1945,
the day I will never forget.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.890
We were ordered out on
Operation Kikusui No.5.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.360
I was deployed as well,
as an Ooka pilot.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.960
Captain, ship trail
confirmed at 12 o'clock.

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:36.870
Take this with you. I know
you wanted it. It's a souvenir.

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:41.010
No, thank you. I won't
be using it anyway.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.240
It's not as heavy as you think.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.880
You're young.
This is all I can do for you.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:22.950
Ironically, the carrier transporting us
took enemy fire and crashed into the sea.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:28.360
Only I survived the crash and an enemy
destroyer saved me from a watery grave.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.700
No!
Stay alive, you...!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:41.470
"Stay alive, you...!"
You are still alive!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.740
I still remember the words
of the sailor who stopped me.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:13.000
Since then, I committed my life to work,
not just for the people of this country...

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:17.340
...but for the people of the world,
for I have already died once.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:23.010
Even if l am thought of
as an unfeeling man...

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:27.140
...l will not ignore
a threat to the people.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.530
Ms. Ochiai.
Yes?

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.470
If you understand now, please go.
I want at least you to survive!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.670
No.
Ms. Ochiai!

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.110
Up

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:52.410
I am secretary to the commander
of the AEGIS Far Eastern branch!

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.880
I cannot leave your side!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.380
Very well! Get in!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.010
Yes, sir!

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.140
Resume attack!

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.850
Target acquired! Target acquired!

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.560
He's catching up to us, Commander!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.370
<i>The Fukuoka-type
invader was the same...</i>

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:40.940
<i>...if a transformed invader has even
a shred of his human memory remaining...</i>

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:05.070
l am... Number One.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.100
Ms. Ochiai!
Yes, sir!

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.150
Hold on tightl!

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:12.210
I am Number One...

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:15.080
NUMBER ONE!!!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.200
NOW!

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.710
It's over.

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.510
Yes.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.340
I am Number One...

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:55.910
I... I am Number One!!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.850
Mr. Nishiya...

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.420
Fire, Ms. Ochai!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.260
Yes, sir!

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.470
In the end...
l am Number One!!

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:06.290
Ms. Ochiai, the radio interference
should be dissipated now.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.990
Contact home base immediately.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:10.220
Yes, sir.

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:12.420
File it as a traffic accident.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:15.400
<i>Mami...</i>

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:21.000
What about Mami? She is waiting
for Mr. Nishiya's return.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.540
Commander!

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:31.740
This is only one unfortunate incident
among countless around the world.

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:33.910
But to me, it's...

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:40.680
It's all right. It's happened a
few times in the past, remember?

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.620
He'll call sooner or later.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:45.860
Yes, I hope so...

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.430
See?

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.660
You were right. I'll get it.

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.770
Hello...

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.100
What?

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:10.620
<i>Itsumademo wasurenai
We received many things</i>

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:14.490
<i>takusan no mono moratta ne.
we will never forget.</i>

00:22:14.590 --> 00:22:19.460
<i>Sora no iro utsushite hikaru
I don't mean the blue jewels flashing</i>

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:22.840
<i>aoi houseki ya
with colors of the sky...</i>

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.970
koinu-tachi
or a big yard

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:30.140
<i>hanemawaru hiroi</i> niwaja <i>nai,
with puppies romping around,</i>

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:33.480
motto motto daijina
but something <i>much</i> more

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:38.110
<i>mono wo.
important.</i>

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:42.980
<i>Kinou Kara kyou e
From yesterday to today,</i>

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:47.620
<i>kyou kara asu e to
from today to tomorrow,</i>

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:54.400
boku-tachi wa aruite yuku yo.
we will walk toward the future.
